---
description: Flutter English and Arabic localization and RTL layout
globs: flutter_app/**
alwaysApply: false
---

The application must support English and Arabic.

Every user-facing string must use the localization system.
Never hardcode user-facing strings inside widgets or business logic.
Use ARB files for English and Arabic.
Localized display strings must remain in the presentation layer.

Never assume an LTR layout.

Use directional APIs where applicable:
- EdgeInsetsDirectional
- AlignmentDirectional
- PositionedDirectional
- start/end instead of left/right
- directional icons where appropriate

Do not use hardcoded left/right spacing for UI that needs RTL support.

Do not concatenate localized strings when grammar or word order can differ
between languages.

Use proper localization APIs for dates, numbers, currency, pluralization,
and formatted messages.
